sec.p:
Natural gas compressor stations maintain the pressure required to transport gas through transmission networks. Where compressors are driven by gas turbines, this function also entails combustion-related emissions, including nitrogen oxides (NO



      x


). The environmental management of these facilities therefore extends beyond fuel consumption and equipment performance to the distribution of pollutants around the station. Nitrogen dioxide (NO



      2


) is particularly relevant to local air quality because of its effects on human health, as reflected in the World Health Organization air quality guidelines [1]. Identifying where turbine emissions produce elevated ambient concentrations is consequently an important component of environmentally responsible operation.
